------Para que Gazebo encuentre mundos y modelos dentro de tu paquete, añade un export en package.xml que agregue rutas a GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH (se hace con <gazebo_ros ... /> en <export>). Lo explica el README de ros_gz_sim. [github.com]

En package.xml (sección <export>):----------------------


<export>
  <build_type>ament_python</build_type>
  <!-- Añade rutas de recursos para Gazebo (modelos/mundos del paquete) -->
  <gazebo_ros gazebo_model_path="${prefix}/models" gazebo_media_path="${prefix}" />
</export>

--------------Y en setup.py, instala worlds/ (y models/ si luego añades modelos propios):----------------------

('share/' + package_name + '/worlds', glob('worlds/*.sdf')),
# si usas modelos:
# ('share/' + package_name + '/models', glob('models/**', recursive=True)),


2) Define un robot diferencial mínimo (URDF) + ros2_control
Crea urdf/bankbot.urdf con un robot básico (cuerpo + 2 ruedas) y ros2_control:



<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot name="bankbot" xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">

  <!-- Base -->
  <link name="base_link">
    <inertial><mass value="5"/><inertia ixx="0.2" iyy="0.2" izz="0.2"/></inertial>
    <visual><geometry><cylinder length="0.25" radius="0.3"/></geometry></visual>
    <collision><geometry><cylinder length="0.25" radius="0.3"/></geometry></collision>
  </link>

  <!-- Ruedas -->
  <link name="wheel_left"/>
  <link name="wheel_right"/>

  <joint name="joint_wheel_left" type="continuous">
    <parent link="base_link"/><child link="wheel_left"/>
    <origin xyz="0 0.25 0" rpy="0 1.5708 0"/>
    <axis xyz="0 1 0"/>
  </joint>

  <joint name="joint_wheel_right" type="continuous">
    <parent link="base_link"/><child link="wheel_right"/>
    <origin xyz="0 -0.25 0" rpy="0 1.5708 0"/>
    <axis xyz="0 1 0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ros2_control: usar gz_ros2_control en Gazebo -->
  <ros2_control name="GazeboSystem" type="system">
    <hardware>
      <plugin>gz_ros2_control/GazeboSystem</plugin>
    </hardware>
    <joint name="joint_wheel_left">
      <command_interface name="velocity"/>
      <state_interface name="position"/>
      <state_interface name="velocity"/>
    </joint>
    <joint name="joint_wheel_right">
      <command_interface name="velocity"/>
      <state_interface name="position"/>
      <state_interface name="velocity"/>
    </joint>
  </ros2_control>

</robot>
----------- gz_ros2_control es el plugin recomendado para Gazebo (moderno) con Humble; hay binarios ros-humble-gz-ros2-control. (Ojo: Gazebo Classic está EOL; no lo uses para proyectos nuevos). [control.ros.org], [control.ros.org]

Configura controladores en config/controllers.yaml:-----------------


controller_manager:
  ros__parameters:
    update_rate: 100

    joint_state_broadcaster:
      type: joint_state_broadcaster/JointStateBroadcaster

    diff_drive_base:
      type: diff_drive_controller/DiffDriveController

diff_drive_base:
  ros__parameters:
    publish_rate: 50.0
    base_frame_id: base_link
    left_wheel_names:  ["joint_wheel_left"]
    right_wheel_names: ["joint_wheel_right"]
    wheel_separation: 0.50
    wheel_radius: 0.10
    cmd_vel_timeout: 0.5
    use_stamped_vel: false
    enable_odom_tf: true


-------En setup.py añade instalación de urdf y config:-------------


('share/' + package_name + '/urdf', glob('urdf/*')),
('share/' + package_name + '/config', glob('config/*.yaml')),


-------3) Launch: Gazebo + mundo + robot + control + RViz
Crea launch/bank_branch_gz.launch.py:-------------


from launch import LaunchDescription
from launch.actions import DeclareLaunchArgument, ExecuteProcess, TimerAction
from launch.substitutions import LaunchConfiguration
from launch_ros.actions import Node
from ament_index_python.packages import get_package_share_directory
import os

def generate_launch_description():
    pkg = get_package_share_directory('bank_robot_bringup')
    world = os.path.join(pkg, 'worlds', 'bank_branch.sdf')
    urdf  = os.path.join(pkg, 'urdf',   'bankbot.urdf')
    ctrl  = os.path.join(pkg, 'config', 'controllers.yaml')

    # 1) Arranca Gazebo (Fortress) con el mundo
    gz = ExecuteProcess(
        cmd=['ign', 'gazebo', '-r', world],
        output='screen'
    )

    # 2) Publica robot_description y spawn en Gazebo vía ros_gz_sim
    rsp = Node(
        package='robot_state_publisher',
        executable='robot_state_publisher',
        name='robot_state_publisher',
        parameters=[{'use_sim_time': True,
                     'robot_description': open(urdf).read()}],
        output='screen'
    )

    # ros_gz_sim: crear entidad desde URDF
    spawn = Node(
        package='ros_gz_sim',
        executable='create',
        arguments=['-file', urdf, '-name', 'bankbot', '-x', '0', '-y', '-2', '-z', '0.15'],
        output='screen'
    )

    # 3) Spawnear controladores sobre el controller_manager de gz_ros2_control
    jsb = Node(
        package='controller_manager',
        executable='spawner',
        arguments=['joint_state_broadcaster', '--controller-manager', '/controller_manager'],
        output='screen'
    )
    dd  = Node(
        package='controller_manager',
        executable='spawner',
        arguments=['diff_drive_base', '--controller-manager', '/controller_manager'],
        output='screen'
    )

    # 4) RViz opcional (usa tu .rviz si quieres)
    rviz = Node(
        package='rviz2', executable='rviz2', output='screen',
        arguments=[]
    )

    return LaunchDescription([
        gz,
        rsp,
        # da 2 s para que arranque el server antes de spawnear
        TimerAction(period=2.0, actions=[spawn]),
        TimerAction(period=4.0, actions=[jsb, dd]),
        # TimerAction(period=6.0, actions=[rviz])  # descomenta si quieres RViz
    ])
El puente ROS↔Gazebo lo proporciona ros_gz/ros_gz_sim y su tooling (create, gz_sim.launch.py, etc.). Mira el README: lanzar Gazebo con ROS y spawnear entidades es exactamente este patrón. [github.com]
El tutorial oficial muestra también cómo puentear tópicos con ros_gz_bridge si lo necesitas (por ejemplo, sensores), con la sintaxis /TOPIC@ROS_MSG@GZ_MSG. [gazebosim.org], [gazebosim.org]


